===Etymology===
{{term|double}} + {{term|whammy}}. The phrase is thought to have been popularized by [[cartoonist]] [[w:Al Capp|Al Capp]] (1909&ndash;1979), from his classic [[comic strip]], ''Li'l Abner''.<!-- from here:
http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Double_Whammy&oldid=413385226 --> 



===Noun===
{{en-noun|double whammies}}
# a [[twofold]] [[blow]] or [[setback]]; a series of two events that cause adverse effects